# Two directories called `dist` are test inputs rather than build output, and
# the bare `dist/` above swallowed both — silently, which is the only way this
# kind of thing ever happens. One is a v1 extension fixture whose manifest names
# `dist/index.js` as its entry; the other is the digest parity tree, which
# contains a `dist` directory precisely to prove that the hash treats it like
# any other name. A negation has to name the directory, not the files in it:
# git does not descend into an excluded directory, so re-including a path under
# one has no effect.
!crates/extension-host/tests/fixtures/*/dist/
!fixtures/extension/digest/tree/dist/
